Think: For each regular file path in usr_empty_check/usr_files.txt, obtain its byte size using stat; write "path size" lines to usr_empty_check/usr_file_sizes.txt and record any failures to usr_empty_check/usr_size_errors.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
 cmd = "stat -c \"%n %s\" \"" $0 "\" 2>/dev/null"
 if ((cmd | getline out) > 0) {
   print out
 } else {
   print $0 >> "usr_empty_check/usr_size_errors.txt"
 }
 close(cmd)
}' usr_empty_check/usr_files.txt > usr_empty_check/usr_file_sizes.txt
